# The read-only root. raspi-config's enable_overlayfs is a thin wrapper over
# overlayroot and installs it from the network at the moment it is asked to -
# which is first boot, on a machine whose network may not be up yet. When that
# apt fails raspi-config still exits 0, so the machine writes overlayroot=tmpfs
# to its kernel command line with nothing installed to act on it and comes up
# writable. Baked in here so first boot needs no network at all.
overlayroot
cryptsetup

